v(40,
  "Those who uproot{H6131} the houses{H1004} of widows{H490} with the falsehood{H8267} of their prayers{H8605} \u2014 for this they shall suffer{H5445} a greater{H1419} penalty on the day{H3117} of judgment{H1779}.",
  [["\u05d0\u05d5\u05ea\u05dd","","those"],["\u05e9\u05e2\u05d5\u05e7\u05e8\u05d9\u05dd","H6131","who uproot"],["\u05d4\u05d1\u05ea\u05d9\u05dd","H1004","the houses"],["\u05d5\u05d4\u05d0\u05dc\u05de\u05e0\u05d5\u05ea","H490","and the widows"],["\u05e2\u05dd","H5973","with"],["\u05e9\u05e7\u05e8","H8267","falsehood of"],["\u05ea\u05e4\u05d9\u05dc\u05d5\u05ea\u05dd","H8605","their prayers"],["\u05d5\u05dc\u05d6\u05d7","","and for this"],["\u05d9\u05e1\u05d1\u05dc\u05d5","H5445","they shall suffer"],["\u05d9\u05d5\u05ea\u05e8","","more"],["\u05e7\u05e0\u05e1","","penalty"],["\u05d2\u05d3\u05d5\u05dc","H1419","great"],["\u05d1\u05d9\u05d5\u05dd","H3117","on the day of"],["\u05d4\u05d3\u05d9\u05df","H1779","judgment"]],
  {"one_way_hebrew":["Uses \u05e2\u05d5\u05e7\u05e8\u05d9\u05dd (oqrim \u2014 'uproot'), from \u05e2\u05e7\u05e8 (aqar, H6131 \u2014 'to uproot'). Greek has \u03ba\u03b1\u03c4\u03b5\u03c3\u03b8\u03af\u03bf\u03bd\u03c4\u03b5\u03c2 ('devouring'). Hebrew: agricultural destruction (uprooting). Greek: consumption (devouring). A back-translator would use \u05d0\u05d5\u05db\u05dc\u05d9\u05dd ('eating'), not the agricultural verb \u05e2\u05e7\u05e8.","Adds \u05d1\u05d9\u05d5\u05dd \u05d4\u05d3\u05d9\u05df ('on the day of judgment'). Greek has merely \u03ba\u03c1\u03af\u03bc\u03b1 ('condemnation'). The Hebrew adds the eschatological Day of Judgment."],"greek_deviations":["Hebrew: 'uproot the houses of widows.' Greek: 'devour widows' houses.'","Hebrew: 'on the day of judgment.' Greek: 'shall receive greater condemnation.'"],"translation_notes":[],"textual_notes":[]}
)

v(41,
  "And Yeshua sat{H3427} before{H6440} [the treasury ark{H727}] where they deposit the treasure{H214} of the Temple{H4720}, and watched{H5027} how the people{H5971} gave their offerings there. And many{H7227} rich{H6223} people gave{H5068} great amounts.",
  [["\u05d5\u05e9\u05d1","H3427","and sat"],["\u05d9\u05e9\u05d5\u05e2","","Yeshua"],["\u05dc\u05e4\u05e0\u05d9","H6440","before"],["\u05d0\u05e8\u05d5\u05df","H727","the ark of"],["\u05d4\u05d0\u05d5\u05e6\u05e8","H214","the treasury"],["\u05de\u05e0\u05d9\u05d7\u05d9\u05dd","H5117","depositing"],["\u05d0\u05d5\u05e6\u05e8","H214","treasure of"],["\u05d4\u05de\u05e7\u05d3\u05e9","H4720","the Temple"],["\u05d5\u05de\u05d1\u05d9\u05d8","H5027","and watching"],["\u05d1\u05d0\u05d9 \u05d6\u05d4","","in which"],["\u05d0\u05d5\u05e4\u05df","","manner"],["\u05d4\u05e2\u05dd","H5971","the people"],["\u05de\u05ea\u05e0\u05d3\u05d1\u05d9\u05dd","H5068","gave offerings"],["\u05e9\u05dd","H8033","there"],["\u05de\u05ea\u05e0\u05d5\u05ea\u05d9\u05d5","","their gifts"],["\u05d5\u05e8\u05d1\u05d9\u05dd","H7227","and many"],["\u05e2\u05e9\u05d9\u05e8\u05d9\u05dd","H6223","rich"],["\u05de\u05ea\u05e0\u05d3\u05d1\u05d9\u05dd","H5068","gave"],["\u05d2\u05d5\u05d3\u05dc","H1419","great"],["\u05d3\u05d1\u05e8\u05d9\u05dd","H1697","amounts"]],
  {"one_way_hebrew":["Uses \u05d0\u05e8\u05d5\u05df \u05d4\u05d0\u05d5\u05e6\u05e8 ('the ark of the treasury'), from \u05d0\u05e8\u05d5\u05df (aron, H727 \u2014 'ark/chest'). This is the same word as the Ark of the Covenant (\u05d0\u05e8\u05d5\u05df \u05d4\u05d1\u05e8\u05d9\u05ea). Greek has \u03b3\u03b1\u05b6\u03bf\u03c6\u03c5\u03bb\u03b1\u03ba\u03af\u03bf\u03bd ('treasury'). A back-translator would use \u05d0\u05d5\u05e6\u05e8 ('treasury'), not \u05d0\u05e8\u05d5\u05df.","Uses \u05de\u05ea\u05e0\u05d3\u05d1\u05d9\u05dd (mitnaddevim \u2014 'giving voluntarily'), from \u05e0\u05d3\u05d1 (nadav, H5068 \u2014 'to volunteer'). This carries the technical sense of the freewill offering (\u05e0\u05d3\u05d1\u05d4 \u2014 Lev 7:16, 22:21). Greek has \u03b2\u03ac\u03bb\u03bb\u03bf\u03bd\u03c4\u03b1 ('casting'). Hebrew emphasizes voluntary nature; Greek is just physical action."],"greek_deviations":["Hebrew: 'treasury ark' (\u05d0\u05e8\u05d5\u05df \u05d4\u05d0\u05d5\u05e6\u05e8). Greek: 'treasury' (\u03b3\u03b1\u05b6\u03bf\u03c6\u03c5\u03bb\u03b1\u03ba\u03af\u03bf\u03bd)."],"translation_notes":["[\u05d0\u05e8\u05d5\u05df \u05d4\u05d0\u05d5\u05e6\u05e8] is bracketed in the source, indicating editorial restoration."],"textual_notes":[]}
)

v(42,
  "And one{H259} poor{H6041} woman{H802} came{H935} and gave willingly{H5068} two small coins.",
  [["\u05d5\u05d1\u05d0\u05d4","H935","and came"],["\u05d0\u05e9\u05d4","H802","a woman"],["\u05d0\u05d7\u05ea","H259","one"],["\u05e2\u05e0\u05d9\u05d9\u05d4","H6041","poor"],["\u05d5\u05e0\u05d3\u05d1\u05d4","H5068","and gave willingly"],["\u05e9\u05ea\u05d9","H8147","two"],["\u05e4\u05e8\u05d5\u05d8\u05d5\u05ea","","small coins"]],
  {"one_way_hebrew":["Uses \u05e4\u05e8\u05d5\u05d8\u05d5\u05ea (perutot \u2014 'small coins'), a specifically Hebrew coin denomination \u2014 the smallest unit in Jewish law. Greek has \u03bb\u03b5\u03c0\u03c4\u1f70 \u03b4\u03cd\u03bf, \u1f45 \u1f10\u03c3\u03c4\u03b9\u03bd \u03ba\u03bf\u03b4\u03c1\u03ac\u03bd\u03c4\u03b7\u03c2 ('two lepta, which is a quadrans'). Greek gives BOTH the Jewish name AND the Roman equivalent. The Hebrew uses only the Jewish denomination, with no Roman conversion \u2014 suggesting a Hebrew-only monetary context."],"greek_deviations":["Hebrew: 'two perutot' (Jewish coins only). Greek: 'two lepta, which is a quadrans' (Jewish + Roman equivalent). Greek adds cross-cultural currency conversion."],"translation_notes":[],"textual_notes":[]}
)

v(43,
  "And Yeshua called{H7121} his disciples and said{H559}: Truly{H571} I say{H559} to you, that poor{H6041} woman gave willingly{H5068} more than all who gave abundantly; for this poor woman gave{H5414} all{H3605} her food{H3978}.",
  [["\u05d5\u05d9\u05e9\u05d5\u05e2","","and Yeshua"],["\u05e7\u05e8\u05d0","H7121","called"],["\u05ea\u05dc\u05de\u05d9\u05d3\u05d9\u05d5","","his disciples"],["\u05d5\u05d0\u05de\u05e8","H559","and said"],["\u05d0\u05de\u05ea","H571","truly"],["\u05d0\u05e0\u05d9","H589","I"],["\u05d0\u05d5\u05de\u05e8","H559","say"],["\u05dc\u05db\u05dd","","to you"],["\u05e9\u05d0\u05d5\u05ea\u05d4","","that"],["\u05e2\u05e0\u05d9\u05d9\u05d4","H6041","poor woman"],["\u05e0\u05d3\u05d1\u05d4","H5068","gave willingly"],["\u05d9\u05d5\u05ea\u05e8","","more"],["\u05de\u05de\u05d4","","than what"],["\u05e9\u05d4\u05dd","","they"],["\u05de\u05e1\u05e4\u05d9\u05e7\u05d9\u05dd","","gave abundantly"],["\u05d0\u05d1\u05dc","","but"],["\u05d6\u05d0\u05ea","H2063","this"],["\u05d4\u05e2\u05e0\u05d9\u05d9\u05d4","H6041","poor woman"],["\u05e0\u05ea\u05e0\u05d4","H5414","gave"],["\u05db\u05dc","H3605","all"],["\u05de\u05d0\u05db\u05dc\u05d4","H3978","her food"]],
  {"one_way_hebrew":["Uses \u05de\u05d0\u05db\u05dc\u05d4 (ma'akhalah \u2014 'her food/sustenance'), from \u05de\u05d0\u05db\u05dc (ma'akhal, H3978 \u2014 'food'). Greek has \u1f45\u03bb\u03bf\u03bd \u03c4\u1f78\u03bd \u03b2\u03af\u03bf\u03bd \u03b1\u1f50\u03c4\u1fc6\u03c2 ('her whole livelihood/life'). The Hebrew is more concrete \u2014 she gave her FOOD. The Greek abstracts to 'livelihood.' A back-translator would use \u05d7\u05d9\u05d9\u05d4 ('her life'), not the concrete 'food.'"],"greek_deviations":["Hebrew: 'all her food' (\u05de\u05d0\u05db\u05dc\u05d4 \u2014 concrete). Greek: 'all her livelihood' (\u03b2\u03af\u03bf\u03c2 \u2014 abstract)."],"translation_notes":[],"textual_notes":[]}
)

